From aa806fd5eabfa9086577bc0f466234706d710626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jraphaelsst <joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:55:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(status_pagina): fan out dev-visibility RLS gate to
 orbity, personal-finance, seed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fans out the social-wiring pilot (feat/status-pagina-dev-visibility,
migration 026/032): status_pagina had exactly ONE SELECT policy
(todos_veem_producao, status='producao'), so the FE's authenticated
product-client read (usePageStatus) never returned a 'desenvolvimento'
row to anyone — not even dev/owner — making the whole desenvolvimento
category dead in production for orbity and personal-finance.

Two additive pieces per target, mirroring the pilot exactly:
- public.current_org_role() (SECURITY DEFINER, symmetric with
  current_org_id(), reads noctus_users.org_role — never user_metadata)
- a SECOND, additive dev_veem_desenvolvimento SELECT policy scoped to
  status='desenvolvimento' AND role IN (owner, dev, admin)

Applied to:
- orbity (015) — bug live, uses public.current_org_id()/noctus_users
- personal-finance (012) — bug live, same trust root
- seed canonical (005, products/seed + templates/product-seed via
  noctus.dev.sync_seed_template) so new scaffolds inherit the fix day-1

Verified against a disposable postgres:16 container per product: applied
each product's full migration chain + the new file, confirmed the policy
and helper exist via pg_policy/pg_proc, and re-applied to confirm
idempotency.

erp-imobiliario SKIPPED — already has "Devs podem ver páginas gerais em
desenvolvimento" + "Admins podem ver todas as páginas" policies since
001_erp_imobiliario.sql, via its own erp.app_role/has_role() model. No
bug live there.

therapy-platform SURFACED out-of-scope — has no noctus_users.org_role
model at all; its role source is therapy.current_user_role() reading
auth.jwt() user_metadata (patient/therapist/clinic-admin business roles,
itself the RLS-never-key-on-user_metadata anti-pattern). Bolting the
org_role-based policy on top would invent a role model the product
doesn't otherwise have.

